 "result": "- **Decorator:** `needs_app_scope` in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It wraps a callback so it runs inside the app context.\n  - Commands registered on `app.cli` (`src/tessel/app.py:338`) or `bundle.cli` (`src/tessel/bundles.py:49`) already have an app context. You don't need the decorator there, and `@app.cli.command()` is enough.\n  - A standalone `AppGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:405`) applies `needs_app_scope` automatically through its `.command()`. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out.\n- **App loader:** `LaunchInfo` in `src/tessel/cli.py:293`. Its `load_app()` method (line 333) finds and loads the app, and `needs_app_scope` calls it via `ctx.ensure_object(LaunchInfo)`.\n- **Top-level group:** `TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`) is the entry-point group. It calls `info.load_app()` to discover app commands (lines 623 and 645).",
